Z||000000||triker||05-30-2000||01:46 PM||||My last e-mail to you was returned, but this may be of interest to some of the forum members. I finally have my shifting probs fixed.  By playing with the governor springs I got my shift point down to 5500 rpms.  A lighter spring under the unweighted side increases the shift point, a heavier spring lowers it.  Well, once I got the wot shift point below the rev limiters 6000 rpm, I realized that I didn't have any second gear.  My trike is so light and pulls so good in third, that I never noticed it before.  Turns out that the intermediate band was worn to the point that it wasn't engaging.  I made a temp repair by lengthening the intermediate actuating pin.  I put the stock spring back in the governor and now the tranny works great!  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||05-31-2000||11:02 AM||||well, that would make it shift funny. glad you got it figured out. I don't know why the mail bounced.||||reg||1
